    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## User Safari FAIL after merged PR #430\n\nThe owner tested the deployed mobile UI on a physical iPhone in Safari (2026-10-14) and explicitly **did not accept** it. PR #430 is already merged/deployed at `main@bcb529931912bb96ea97df8ed8fb9a3e3d6ba7d8`; never rewrite that merged PR. New isolated UI-only fix.\n\n### Acceptance contract (all three mandatory)\n\n1. **Profile-specific tab title.** Current mobile tab `#mobileTabBattles` hardcodes `Баттлы`, while the active renderer-owned `#battlesHeader .battleTitleText` displays `Споры` for the tested UI tone. The visible mobile tab title MUST track the current game's actual panel title for each tone/profile, while retaining its count and accurate accessible name. The authoritative renderer may update the title at runtime; avoid new independent copy tables/hardcoded single-tone string. Keep other tab titles, counts, and focus keyboard behavior correct.\n\n2. **Remove duplicate mobile section headers, reclaim height.** The second row below the three-tab strip currently renders `#battlesHeader` as `Споры (1)`; equivalents are `#dmBlockHeader` and `#eventsHeader`. On mobile only (<=860px), visually remove duplicate outer panelHeader rows, leaving the permanent tab strip followed immediately by visible authorized panel content. Do NOT delete those header nodes or counters from DOM: game renderers still write counters and panel state there. Do not remove legitimate DM recipient/thread navigation (`#dmHeader`) or hide battle/event action controls. Preserve desktop headers and closed DM / gated .hidden logic, legacy persisted panel--collapsed overrides, panel scroll and accessibility.\n\n3. **Real horizontal swipe on lower content.** In physical iOS Safari, horizontal swipe does not change tabs, while vertical scroll works. Investigate pointer/touch/cancel path and true hit targets. Current `ui-mobile.js` `INTERACTIVE` includes whole `.battleCard,.eventCard` and `contentPanelFromTarget()` requires `.panelBody`; on card-filled screens `isInteractiveStart` rejects many genuine swipes. Allow horizontal left/right tab gestures starting on non-control regions of visible card/content; do not hijack taps on buttons/inputs/selects/interactive card actions, draggable elements, genuine horizontal carousels, inner DM horizontal scrollers or vertical scrolling. Use direction/threshold arbitration, avoid synthetic click activations after a swipe, preserve swipe from an initially closed/empty DM panel, and avoid interfering with Safari edge navigation if applicable. Diagnose `pointercancel`/gesture stream rather than assuming simulated PointerEvents prove iOS behavior.\n\n### Source pointers (verify current repository files, not assumed fixed paths)\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/index.html`: `#mobilePanelTabs` contains literal `Баттлы`.\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-mobile.js`: `INTERACTIVE`, `isInteractiveStart`, `contentPanelFromTarget`, `startSwipe/moveSwipe/endSwipe`, `updateCounters`; count observer does not currently observe the battle-title text.\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/mobile-ui.css`: `#dmBlock/#battlesBlock/#eventsBlock .panelHeader`, `touch-action:pan-y`, mobile-only layout.\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-battles.js`: renderer updates `#battlesHeader .battleTitleText` at runtime; it is the source of the observed profile name.\n- `tools/test_mobile_first_interface.html` and `tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`: existing tests mostly dispatch synthetic PointerEvents, which missed real iOS Safari FAIL.\n\n### Workflow and evidence\n\nCodex is the only implementer. Check current `AGENTS.override.md`, `AGENTS.md`, applicable policies, `TASKS.md`, `PROJECT_MEMORY.md`, `.ai-memory/**`, latest main, concurrent PRs and worktree occupancy before execution. Work in a NEW isolated branch + Draft PR, not directly main. Do not modify unrelated Stage 7.15 logic/economy, onboarding tone copy PR #433, or any user's data. Mirror every runtime change in `docs/**` and test blob parity.\n\nAdd executable regressions checking dynamic five-tone tab title + aria-label and count; duplicate header rows truly zero height on mobile and remain on desktop; real touch-like gestures on card text vs button with vertical/horizontal arbitration, empty DM and horizontal scrollers, state unchanged and no accidental click. If real iOS Safari cannot be automated, explicitly note the limitation and require owner Safari retest. Run appropriate static, DOM, JS, mirror, CI; report exact PR HEAD and proof. **Do not merge or claim Safari PASS** without ChatGPT review and owner acceptance.\n\nNo screenshot or personal in-game chat data attached to this public issue.",
